@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@recordId = 1

### List employees
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees?page=0&size=10

### Search and filter together
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees?search=rao&department=Engineering&status=ACTIVE&page=0&size=5

### Add an employee. Use the returned numeric id in later requests.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeId": "EMP-200",
  "fullName": "Amit Shah",
  "email": "amit.shah@example.com",
  "phone": "+91 98765 43000",
  "department": "Engineering",
  "designation": "Backend Developer",
  "dateOfJoining": "2025-08-12",
  "salary": 600000.00,
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### View one employee
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/{{recordId}}

### Edit an employee
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/{{recordId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeId": "EMP-200",
  "fullName": "Amit Shah",
  "email": "amit.shah@example.com",
  "phone": "+91 98765 43000",
  "department": "Engineering",
  "designation": "Software Engineer",
  "dateOfJoining": "2025-08-12",
  "salary": 650000.00,
  "status": "INACTIVE"
}

### List saved departments
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/departments

### Count employees
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/summary

### Export matching employees
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/export?department=Engineering&status=ACTIVE

### Delete an employee
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/{{recordId}}
